Render a valid JSON Schema for no-argument tools (never "parameters": null).

ToolsFunctionInput::renderFunctionArray() emits `'parameters' => NULL` for any
function that declares no properties. On the wire that becomes
`"function": {"name": "...", "parameters": null}`.

OpenAI's own endpoint tolerates that, so it goes unnoticed — but an
OpenAI-*compatible* proxy need not. Sending it to a LiteLLM proxy in front of an
Anthropic model fails the entire request, not just the offending tool:

  litellm.APIConnectionError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'get'
    File ".../litellm/llms/anthropic/chat/transformation.py", line 659,
      in _map_tool_helper
    if _input_schema.get("type") != "object":
       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

Every OpenAI-based provider in this module hits it (the payload is built in
OpenAiBasedProviderClientBase), and it only takes one no-argument tool in the
set — a legitimate thing for a tool to be — to break every request that offers
tools.

Emit `{"type": "object"}` instead, which is a valid (and empty) argument schema
for every provider. `properties` is omitted rather than emitted empty because an
empty PHP array JSON-encodes as `[]`, not the `{}` the schema calls for; both the
Anthropic and OpenAI schemas treat it as optional.

Also fixes ToolsPropertyInput::renderPropertyArray(), which derives an array
property's `items` from this method's `parameters` and so produced `items: null`
for an empty child object.

--- a/src/OperationType/Chat/Tools/ToolsFunctionInput.php
+++ b/src/OperationType/Chat/Tools/ToolsFunctionInput.php
@@ -136,16 +136,23 @@
     foreach ($this->properties as $property) {
       $properties[$property->getName()] = $property->renderPropertyArray();
     }
+    // Always render a valid JSON Schema object, even for a function that takes
+    // no arguments. A NULL here reaches the provider as "parameters": null,
+    // which OpenAI-compatible endpoints tolerate but stricter consumers do not
+    // — the LiteLLM proxy's Anthropic transformation calls ->get() on the
+    // schema and dies with "'NoneType' object has no attribute 'get'", so a
+    // single no-argument tool breaks the whole request. "properties" is left
+    // out rather than emitted empty, because an empty PHP array JSON-encodes
+    // as [] and the schema calls for {}.
     $function = [
       'name' => $this->name,
       'description' => $this->description,
-      'parameters' => NULL,
+      'parameters' => [
+        'type' => 'object',
+      ],
     ];
     if (!empty($properties)) {
-      $function['parameters'] = [
-        'type' => 'object',
-        'properties' => $properties,
-      ];
+      $function['parameters']['properties'] = $properties;
       foreach ($this->getRequiredProperties() as $property) {
         $function['parameters']['required'][] = $property->getName();
       }
